1 NOTE <p>Obituary:&nbsp;</p>
<p>Age 62, of Morningside, went into the Lord's arms peacefully on Sunday, June 10, 2012 after a courageous battle with cancer. Preceded in death by parents Patrick and Mary Sw
2 CONC eeney; and brother Frank Sweeney. Dear sister of Patricia (James) Maloney, James (Mary) Sweeney, Marjorie (Raymond) Webber, Father John Sweeney and sister-in-law Charlene Sweeney; beloved and admired 
2 CONC aunt, "A.K.", of nieces Karen Larned, Diana Backner, Melissa Cook, Dana Allwein and Sheila Evans; nephews Daniel, David, Douglas, Patrick, and Christopher Sweeney, and James, Donald, Michael, Sean, an
2 CONC d Gerard Maloney; 33 great-nieces and nephews and two great-great-nieces. Will be missed by many loving cousins, friends, co-workers, and neighbors, especially Bernadette Gable. Kathy completed a 37 y
2 CONC ear career at Shadyside Hospital, finishing as Lead Tech. of the A.T.L. The family thanks Dr. Daniel Petro and his oncology team and Dr. Gregory Kubicek and Dr. Katie Nason, thoracic surgeon and the c
2 CONC aring and compassionate staff of Vincentian Skilled Nursing. In lieu of flowers, contributions may be made to "Autism Speaks", 8035 McKnight Rd., Suite 301, Pittsburgh, PA 15237. Friends received at M
2 CONC cCABE BROS, INC., FUNERAL HOME, 5300 Penn Ave., Bloomfield on Tuesday and Wednesday 1-4 and 6-8 where funeral will commence on Thursday at 9 a.m. followed by Mass of Christian Burial in St. Bonaventur
2 CONC e Church at 10 a.m. - See more at: http://www.legacy.com/obituaries/postgazette/obituary.aspx?pid=157995144#sthash.QVI3r7G7.dpuf</p>
