1 NOTE &amp;lt;p&amp;gt;Was not married.&nbsp; Worked for a Mrs Griscom in the Walled Gardens in Haverford.&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;
&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;Struggling a bit on this one.&nbsp; She made numerous trips over
2 CONC  and back to Ireland in the 1920s and 1930s (records available).&nbsp; She was sponsored by a Mrs Griscom each time.&nbsp; I spoke to her nephew Jim Shiels in November 2017 but I can't recall if he sa
2 CONC id she wasn't married or if she married Leon Belcher.&nbsp; I have a comment added to say she was not married but I am sure Jim Shiels told me she married Leon.&nbsp; Leon has plenty records available
2 CONC  and was pending divorce when he enlisted for WW1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;
&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;Her age is also causing confusion, she may have had to lie about her age to move as she moved away in 
2 CONC her late 20s it seems.&nbsp; She is listed as being 10 years younger in certain records however her birth record is 1893.&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;
