1 NOTE <p>Born in Balloor in presence of Aunt Bridget Shiels. Father's profession listed as chaffeur. I found the following extract online:</p>
<p><span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source Sans Pro'
2 CONC , 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px;">Minch Park in Parkesburg, PA was named after the Minch Family. Mathew Minch worked as a gardener in 1920 and in 1930 for a the Beale Family. Th
2 CONC is was Horace Beale, one of the richest people in chester county at the time.</span><br style="box-sizing: inherit; color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source Sans Pro', 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
2 CONC  font-size: 16px;" /><span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source Sans Pro', 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px;">I also found Hannah and Catherine and Thomas in Ellis Island Au
2 CONC gust 20, 1916 traveling back from ireland. Having the birth dates and places where born. Catherine was born May 1904, Parkesburg, PA and Thomas was Born May 1, 1908 in ballure Ireland.</span></p>
<p>
2 CONC Thomas registered for WW2, worked at&nbsp;<span style="background-color: #f3f0e9; color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source Sans Pro', 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px;">Lukens Steel Co
2 CONC .</span></p>
<p><span style="background-color: #f3f0e9; color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source Sans Pro', 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px;">Thomas died as a result of an accidental
2 CONC  fire caused by explosion of oil heater. Trapped in burning house and burned to death. Bookeeper by trade. Divorced.</span></p>
