 OBITUARY for &amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Mary&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt; &amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Ko
4 CONC ehler&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt;; date of birth: 1939-08-06; recent
residence: Newtown Square, PA; published by Rothermel-Videon Funeral Home. &amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Mary&amp;lt;/span&am
4 CONC p;gt; &amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Anita&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt; &amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Koehler&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt;, 81, of Malvern, PA, passed away November 12, 2020.
4 CONC  
Born August 6, 1939 in Philadelphia, PA, she was the daughter of the late Edward and Anna (nee Dunne) Kelly.

&amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Mary&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt; had many interests
4 CONC . First and foremost, she was proud of her Irish heritage and consumed many
books on Irish history. &amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Mary&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt; also loved to read fiction an
4 CONC d especially loved solving crossword
puzzles. In fact, you could always find her with a crossword puzzle book wherever she went in case the conversation got boring. She turned
her hand to various ar
4 CONC tistic endeavors over the years, including writing a 1,000 page draft of an Irish-American generational saga, sewing
clothes, baking bread (before it was a popular pastime), and other crafts. &amp;lt;
4 CONC span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Mary&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt; was also a
connoisseur of teas – she was a regular at the Simpson House Tea Room and some of the other tea houses around the area. Final
4 CONC ly, she
begrudgingly became an Eagles and Penn State football fan after she was subjected to watching the games with her husband and son.   

&amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Mary&amp;lt;/
4 CONC span&amp;gt; worked for Northwest Airlines in Philadelphia when she was young, through which she had the
opportunity to travel and see the world. After settling down in West Bradford to raise kids, s
4 CONC he worked on the staff at Dr. Trievel Family
Medicine of Lionville, PA until her retirement.

She was the loving mother of Karen A. &amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Koehler&amp;lt;/span&amp;
4 CONC gt; (James Cresmer), Sheila K. &amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Koehler&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt; (Brett Aukburg), and Thomas C. &amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Koehler&amp;lt;/span&am
4 CONC p;gt; (Eliza) and
grandmother of Alexandra, Amelia, and Ian.  She was also sister to Edward Kelly (Carol) and Michael Kelly (Linda). She was
predeceased by her husband Arthur T. &amp;lt;span class="h
4 CONC ighlight-text"&amp;gt;Koehler&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt;, her son, Casey E. &amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Koehler&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt;, and brother, Thomas Kelly.

Services and interment are pr
4 CONC ivate due to COVID-19.
