2 NOTE Wayne A. Allridge Jr. Wayne A. Allridge, Jr., 28, of Leander, formerly of Monongahela, PA, died on Monday, November 8, 2004, in Austin after a two year battle against Hodgkin s Disease. He was born Oc
3 CONC tober 26, 1966, in New Eagle, PA, a son of Wayne A. Allridge, Sr., and Barbara J. Marvenko Allridge who survive and continue to reside in Monongahela. Mr. Allridge worked as a technical support analys
3 CONC t for Dell, Inc. and attended Gateway Community Church in Austin. He was a 1984 graduate of Ringgold High School in Monongahela, PA, and earned his bachelor of science degree from Thiel College. He wa
3 CONC s also a member of MENSA. In spite of his illness, he was always humorous and remained diligent to his family, friends, and employer. He will be greatly missed, but we all know he is with Christ. Surv
3 CONC iving him are his beloved wife, Carole M. Brennan Allridge, whom he married on November 21, 1998 at the University Christian Church in Austin; one son, Alexsei P. Allridge, at home; one brother, Micha
3 CONC el Allridge and wife, Jodi, of Bethel Park, PA; two nephews, Elijah and Aidan Allridge; and one uncle, Marshall S. Marvenko of Charleroi, PA. Carole and Alexsei Allridge wish to invite all friends and
3 CONC  loved ones to a celebration of Wayne s life at Gateway Community Church, 4300 Bull Creek Road, Austin, Texas, on Tuesday, November 23, 2004, at 7:00 p.m. In lieu of flowers, the family requests contr
3 CONC ibutions be made to the Mario Lemieux Foundation, 920 Fort Duquesne Blvd., Pittsburgh, PA, 15222, or a blood donation to the Blood and Tissue Center of Central Texas.
