2 NOTE Wayne A. Allridge Sr., 72, of Monongahela, died Thursday, February 11, 2016, in Monongahela Valley Hospital.
He was born January 18, 1944, in Pittsburgh, a son of Albert J. and Thelma Coleman Allridge
3 CONC .
Mr. Allridge had worked for 34 years as a data systems support manager for the Federal Reserve Bank in Pittsburgh until his retirement in 2004.
Following his graduation in 1961 from Monongahela High
3 CONC  School, he went on to earn a bachelor's degree in psychology with a minor in math from W&J College and a master's degree in psychology from Duquesne University.
He had served four years stateside in 
3 CONC the U.S. Navy during the Vietnam War.
Mr. Allridge was a member of Mingo Creek Presbyterian Church.
He loved woodworking, gardening, working on his antique cars, and most of all, his grandchildren.
Su
3 CONC rviving are his wife of 50 years, Barbara J. Marvenko Allridge, who he married July 10, 1965; a son and daughter-in-law, Michael and Jodi Allridge of Bethel Park; three grandchildren, Elijah, Aidan an
3 CONC d Alexsei Allridge; and a brother-in-law, Marshall Marvenko of Washington.
Deceased is a son, Wayne A. "J.R." Allridge, who died November 8, 2004.
Friends will be received from noon to 4 p.m. Sunday i
3 CONC n Marshall Marra Funeral Home, 216 Chess Street, Monongahela, 724-258-6767, www.marshallmarrafuneralhome.com. Services will be held at 11 a.m. Monday, February 15, in Mingo Creek Presbyterian Church, 
3 CONC Finleyville, with the Rev. Glenn McClelland officiating. Anyone wishing to attend the service, please go directly to the church. Interment will follow in Monongahela Cemetery with military honors cond
3 CONC ucted by Mon-Valley Honor Guard and Firing Squad.
Memorial donations can be made to the Mingo Creek Presbyterian Church (Building Fund), 500 Mingo Creek Road, Finleyville, PA 15332. - See more at: htt
3 CONC p://m.legacy.com/obituaries/observer-reporter/obituary.aspx?n=&pid=177706050&referrer=0&preview=True#sthash.A7FVVlOY.dpuf
