3 TEXT Suzanne S. McDonough&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;Birth: Oct 2 1936&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;Death: Dec 18 2012&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;Burial: Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;Notes: SUZANNE S. (CALLAHAN) McDONOUGH Ag
4 CONC e 76, wife of Michael J. McDonough, passed away peacefully on Tuesday, December 18, 2012, surrounded by her children. She was born in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania to Frank and Sarah Callahan who emigrated
4 CONC  together from Ireland in 1921. An only child, Suzanne had an unwavering love for her parents and was dearly cherished by them. She attended Homewoods Holy Rosary Grade School and graduated from Sacre
4 CONC d Heart High School. On June 11, 1960, Suzanne married Michael, an Irishman from Galway who came to the United States in 1955 at the age of 24. They raised seven children at their home in Wilkinsburg.
4 CONC  A loving and committed mother who delighted in her childrens successes, Suzanne worked for more than 30 years at Columbia/LifeCare. Central to their social life was raising their children in the Iris
4 CONC h culture, which included picnicking and swimming at the Irish Centre of Pittsburgh, Sunday Irish breakfasts, and years of lessons and competitions with the Burke School of Irish Dance. Suzanne is sur
4 CONC vived by her husband, Michael; and her seven children, John McDonough (Dawn German), Suzanne Coglio (Jeff), Catherine McDonough, Maureen LaFace, Sally McDonough Niemiec, Eileen McDonough, and Mary McD
4 CONC onough-Paul (David Paul); and nine grandchildren, Scott, Justin, Brad, Devin, Riley, Sarah Grace, Liam, Quinn, and Cian. Visitation will be held on Thursday, December 20, 2012 from 2:00 to 8:00 p.m. a
4 CONC t THOMAS NIED FUNERAL HOME, INC., 7441 Washington Street, Swissvale. Mass of Christian Burial will be held in the St. James Catholic Church Wilkinsburg, at 10:30 a.m. on Friday, December 21, 2012. Mem
4 CONC orial donations may be made to St. James Catholic Church, 718 Franklin Avenue, Wilkinsburg, PA 15221. www.niedfuneralhome.com
