4 CONC p;gt;Text: 
 OBITUARY for Arthur Koehler; recent residence: Downingtown,
PA; published by Donohue Funeral Home-Downingtown (formerly Ralston & Bredickas FH). Arthur
Thomas Koehler, 83, of Malvern, pas
4 CONC sed away September 27, 2018.
Born September 6, 1935 in Philadelphia, PA, he was a son of the late Fredrick and Katherine (nee Neary) Koehler. He served honorably in the U.S. Air Force. Arthur was a
me
4 CONC mber of West Caln Sportsman Club and Cacoosing Gun Club and Range. He enjoyed hunting, skeet shooting and was an avid Eagles and Penn
State fan. He loved trips to the Happy Days Diner and spending tim
4 CONC e with his family and friends. Arthur worked for Boeing Vertol for several years before settling in with a career as a phone technician
with Bell Telephone and Verizon. He was the beloved husband of M
4 CONC ary A. (nee Kelly) Koehler;
loving father of Karen A. Koehler (James Cresmer), Sheila K. Koehler (Brett Aukburg), and Thomas C. Koehler (Eliza); and adoring grandfather of Alexandra, Ian, and Amelia. 
4 CONC He was predeceased by his son,
Casey E. Koehler and his six siblings. Relatives and friends are invited to his Visitation 10-10:50
AM on Wednesday, October 3, 2018 at St. Joseph's Catholic Church, 332
4 CONC  Manor Ave, Downingtown, PA 19335, 610- 269-8294, with his Funeral Mass
to follow at 11 AM. Interment at St. Joseph Cemetery. In lieu of flowers, contributions may be made to Disabled American Veteran
4 CONC s Charitable
Service Trust, https://cst.dav.org. Arr. by The Donohue Funeral Home, 43 W. Lancaster Avenue, Downingtown, PA 19335, 610-269-3080. Online
condolences www.donohuefuneralhome.com.
