1 NOTE <p>George's existence is initially signalled by the local reference in Fanad to his son as "Donie Seoirse". This was noted by several local sources, including Uncle John and Big Paddy Callaghan. There
2 CONC  are three written records of this name which support his existence:</p><p><p>1. A record for "George Freil" in the 1834 Tithe Applotments for Ballymichael</p></p><p><p>2. A record for "George Friel" 
2 CONC farming 10a 3r 10p in Ballymichael in Griffith's Primary Valuation in 1851</p></p><p><p>3. A death record for a "Georgius Friel" in Ballymichael on 16 May 1865 in the Clondavaddog Parish Records.</p><
2 CONC /p><p><p>There is also a record of a George Friel as a witness at the wedding of John Friel and Bridget McElwaine on 28 February 1852 in Clondavaddog. The other witness was a Catherine Gallagher - was
2 CONC  she his wife?.</p><p><p>[FT_Art_Na_MAacioch.FTW]</p></p><p><p></p></p><p><p>George's existence is initially signalled by the local reference in Fanad to his son as "Donie Seoirse". This was noted by 
2 CONC several local sources, including Uncle John and Big Paddy Callaghan. There are three written records of this name which support his existence:</p><p><p>1. A record for "George Freil" in the 1834 Tithe
2 CONC  Applotments for Ballymichael</p></p><p><p>2. A record for "George Friel" farming 10a 3r 10p in Ballymichael in Griffith's Primary Valuation in 1851</p></p><p><p>3. A death record for a "Georgius Frie
2 CONC l" in Ballymichael on 16 May 1865 in the Clondavaddog Parish Records.</p></p><p>There is also a record of a George Friel as a witness at the wedding of John Friel and Bridget McElwaine on 28 February 
2 CONC 1852 in Clondavaddog. The other witness was a Catherine Gallagher - was she his wife?.
