4 CONC Eleanor Grace, James Daniel, and Henry Presant; and Knox and Riverleigh McDonnell. Predeceased by
parents Kathryn (Miller) and Abe &amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Schwartz&amp;lt;/span&amp;
4 CONC gt; and brother Richard. Survived by brother Irv
(Jeannie Greenblatt). Survived by nephew David  Winer, nieces Wendi &amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Schwartz&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt;, Lisa Frit
4 CONC z, and
Cindy Marselis-Lundeen. Also survived by great and grand nieces and  nephews. Born July 19, 1930, in Long Branch, NJ. Raised in Asbury Park,
Chester, and Philadelphia. Drafted into the Army in 
4 CONC 1952; stationed in Munich, Germany instead of the Korean war zone. Earned BA in Business
from Temple U on the GI Bill. Worked for the City of Philadelphia, Philco, and Lit Brothers' before a 33-year c
4 CONC areer with RCA/GE, retiring
in 1992 as Manager of Proposals. The family enjoyed living in Florida in the early years of the space program while he worked for RCA on
Patrick Air Force Base.  Traveled e
4 CONC xtensively for RCA/GE, including Brazil, Alaska, Puerto Rico, and Ascension Island. Lived in Voorhees for
 34 years before moving to New Freedom Village in Berlin in 2001, then recently All American A
