 OBITUARY for Anne Finley, nicknamed Nancy; recent residence: Sea Isle City, NJ; published by Rone Funeral Service-Vi
4 CONC neland. Anne "Nancy"
Finley AGE: 82 • Sea Isle City Anne "Nancy" (&amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Ryan&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt;) Finley, 82 of Sea Isle City, NJ, passed
away peacefully at hom
4 CONC e, surrounded by her loved ones, on Sunday, March 5, 2017. Nancy was born in Philadelphia, PA, on May 12, 1934 to
Phillip and &amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Maryann&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt; (M
4 CONC artin) &amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Ryan&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt;. Nancy was raised on
Melon Street in Philadelphia, receiving her education at Saint Agatha's Elementary School and West Cath
4 CONC olic High School. Nancy attended
Misericordia School of Nursing and received her license as a Registered Nurse in May 1958. She began her career as a nurse in the labor and
delivery room at Misericord
4 CONC ia General Hospital. Nancy married the love of her life, Peter J. Finley, on November 22, 1958. Nancy and Pete
raised their five children in Vineland, NJ, where they were active members of Sacred Hear
4 CONC t Parish. Nancy worked as a labor and delivery room
nurse at Newcomb Hospital in Vineland. She received a Bachelor of Arts Degree in School Nursing from Glassboro State College in June 1978.
Nancy wor
4 CONC ked as a school nurse for the Vineland Board of Education at the D'Ippolito and Johnstone schools until her retirement in June
1999. Nancy loved the hundreds of children she cared for during her 20 ye
4 CONC ars as a school nurse. Nancy and Pete retired to Sea Isle City in
2008. Nancy was devoted to her family, was a wonderful cook and enjoyed hosting gatherings at her homes in Vineland and Sea Isle. Nanc
4 CONC y
dearly loved and was very proud of her grandchildren. They brought her countless hours of happiness. Nancy was an avid collector of nursing
statues and gladly shared her stories behind each of her m
4 CONC ore than 250 statues with anyone who asked. She loved creating unique and special
handmade gifts for her family. Nancy loved Irish music and culture, celebrating many of it's traditions with her famil
4 CONC y. She was a fabulous
cookie baker, passing her skills down through two generations of her family and creating lasting happy memories for her grandchildren
through the annual holiday baking extravagan
4 CONC za. Nancy loved to travel especially with her family and visited dozens of places in the United
States and around the world, including many times to Ireland. She is survived by husband of 58 years, Pe
4 CONC ter; her five children, Peter
(Coleen), Kathleen (Orlando "Nick" Riveria), Anne, Patrick, and Matthew (Leigh); six grandchildren, Danielle Opperman
(Danny), Colleen, Kylie, Brennan, Meghan and Michell
4 CONC e Milita-Freeman (Jon); two wonderful caregivers, Brittani Gillice and Liz
Larkin. Nancy was predeceased by her parents, Phillip and &amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Maryann&amp;lt;/span&amp
4 CONC ;gt; &amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Ryan&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt; and her brother, Daniel &amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Ryan&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt;. At Nancy's request, services and
4 CONC 
burial will be private. Arrangements are under the supervision of Rone Funeral Service, 1110 East Chestnut Avenue, Vineland, NJ 08360. In
lieu of flowers donations in memory of Nancy may be made to: 
4 CONC 1. Covenant House of Atlantic City, 929 Atlantic Avenue, Atlantic City, NJ
08401 2. Sacred Heart of Camden School, 1739 Ferry Avenue, Camden, NJ 08104 To send online condolences please visit our websi
4 CONC te at
www.RONEFUNERALSERVICE.com or mail them to: P.O. Box 513, Sea Isle City, New Jersey 08243.
