4 CONC an McGinley (born Cannon)&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;Obituary publication: May 19 2022 - Springfield, Pennsylvania, United States&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;Text: 
 OBITUARY for Henry J. Cannon; date of birth: 1942-06-14
4 CONC ; recent residence: Springfield, PA; published by O'Leary Funeral Home Ltd..
Henry J. Cannon, of Havertown, died on May 19, 2022, at his home in Havertown, PA.                                        

4 CONC Born June 14, 1942, in West Philadelphia, Henry was the son of the late Henry Cannon and the late Mary
(McElwaine) Cannon, both of whom were born in Fanad, County Donegal, Ireland. Henry was the broth
4 CONC er of the late Mary Cannon Walters & Margaret Mary (Peggy) Cannon Brennan.
Henry was a graduate of St Agatha’s grade school in West Philadelphia and a 1960 graduate of St. Thomas More High School.
H
4 CONC enry was a proud Vietnam era veteran of the US Army with most of his military service spent in Germany.
Mr. Cannon spent his entire working career as a federal employee at the US Naval Base, Philadelp
4 CONC hia. He retired in 1995, after 35 years of
service. Among the positions he held was as an equal employment opportunity officer of the naval station. He also held the position of head
of support servic
4 CONC es. His last position was at the human resource office.
Henry was very active in various Irish organizations and so proud of his Irish heritage, making many trips to his parents’birthplace. He
was p
4 CONC ast president of the Donegal Society of Philadelphia; past president of the Philadelphia Ceili Group; former member of the board of
directors of the Commodore Barry Club, (Irish Center) and former mem
4 CONC ber of the Federation of Irish Societies.
He is survived by his sister; Susan Cannon McGinley of Havertown, as well as 6 nieces, 5 nephews, 17 grand nieces and nephews & 6
great-grand nieces and nephe
4 CONC ws.
Relatives and friends are invited to his Viewing Tuesday, May 24, 2022, 6:00 pm – 8:00 pm, O’Leary Funeral Home, 640 E.
Springfield Rd. Springfield PA 19064 and Wednesday, May 25, 2022, 9:30am
4 CONC  Sacred Heart Church, Manoa and Shelbourne Rds. Havertown, PA
19083. Mass of Christian Burial, May 25, 2022, 10:30 am in the Church. Burial SS Peter & Paul Cemetery.
Donations in Henry’s honor can b
4 CONC e given to the National Centre for Padre Pio, 111 Barto Road, Barto PA 19504. info@padrepio.org
To send flowers to the family or plant a tree in memory of Henry J. Cannon, please visit our floral stor
4 CONC e.
