4 CONC  OBITUARY for Margaret Rushkin; recent residence: Roseville,
CA; published by Blue Oaks Cremation & Burial Services. Margaret Rushkin passed away peacefully to be with the lord on Sunday, January 19, 
4 CONC 2020 at the age of 89 after a long
struggle with Alzheimer's. She was born on May 15, 1930 to James P and Hellen M McCaul in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. She had two siblings,
Ellen Panetta and James P M
4 CONC cCaul II. Margaret was an extremely talented musician and attended Carnegie
Technical Institute (Now CMU) on a music scholarship, receiving a double Bachelor's degree in Music Education and in Harp, g
4 CONC raduating
Suma Kum Laude. She later received her Masters degree in Music performance. Margaret held the position
of President of the Sacramento Saturday Club a non-profit who provides scholarships to 
4 CONC worthy musicians. She was also the Keyboardist for
the Sacramento Symphony playing piano and the Celeste. She was a part time faculty member at California State University, Sacramento and had
held pos
4 CONC itions as a teacher for both elementary and high school at several cities throughout her career. Additionally, she has taught
numerous piano students over a 50+ years career. She met her husband Walla
4 CONC ce, employed at that time with the Pittsburgh Symphony in 1955 and
they were married on July 28th in Virginia. She was a loving mother to three children, Cynthia Marie, Christopher Wallace, and Suzann
4 CONC e
Elaine. Friends of Margaret, please feel welcome to celebrate her life with us at her memorial service
at St. Augustine's of Canterbury, 1800 Wildcat Blvd, Rocklin, CA 95675 at 3:00 PM on Friday, Ja
4 CONC nuary 31st.
