&amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;McHugh&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt;, Kay Hastings and the late Rita Weik, John, Charles and Joseph &a
4 CONC mp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;McHugh&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt;. Bob was a U.S. Army Korean War Veteran. He was a proud Phila. Firefighter of 34 years, working at
Engine 27 as Battalion Chief 3's
4 CONC  Aide, and as Deputy Chief 3/2's Aide for over 2 decades, and was a member of the League of the Sacred
Heart. He retired in 1992. After retirement he worked full time as a security guard at Nazareth H
4 CONC ospital. Bob was also an employee of Sears
and Roebuck for decades. He coached baseball and soccer at Torresdale Boys' Club and was a referee with the United Junior Soccer League.
