4 CONC ce: PA; published by Burns Funeral Home-Frankford Ave.. McHUGH ROBERT P. on July 15, 2010,
age 77. Resident of Phila., born and raised in Bristol, PA. Beloved husband of Margaret (nee McStravock). Dev
4 CONC oted father of Bob
(Janet), Meg Houseman (Jim), John (Lori) and Gerard (Janet) McHugh. Proud Pop of Megan, Rob, Meganne (Tom),
Patrick (Nora), Courtney, Shane, Molly, Logan, Kelly, Ryan, Matthew, Coll
4 CONC in and Kaitlyn, great grandfather of Seretha. Son of the late
William and Seretha McHugh. Dear brother of William and James McHugh, &amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Kay&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt; 
4 CONC &amp;lt;span class="highlight-text"&amp;gt;Hastings&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt; and the late Rita Weik, John, Charles and Joseph McHugh. Bob was a U.S. Army Korean War Veteran. He
was a proud Phila. Firefigh
4 CONC ter of 34 years, working at Engine 27 as Battalion Chief 3's Aide, and as Deputy Chief 3/2's Aide for over 2
decades, and was a member of the League of the Sacred Heart. He retired in 1992. After reti
4 CONC rement he worked full time as a security guard at
Nazareth Hospital. Bob was also an employee of Sears and Roebuck for decades. He coached baseball and soccer at Torresdale Boys' Club and
was a refere
4 CONC e with the United Junior Soccer League. Relatives, friends and members of Local #22 are invited to his Viewing Tuesday eve. 6-9
P.M. and Wednesday, 8:30-9:15 A.M. at the BURNS FUNERAL HOME, 9708 Frank
4 CONC ford Ave. (So. of Grant Ave.) followed by his Funeral
Mass, 10 A.M. St. Katherine of Siena Church. Int. Resurrection Cem. In lieu of flowers donations in his memory may be made to the Hero
Scholarship
