4 CONC ;lt;br&amp;gt; &amp;lt;br&amp;gt;LifeSketch: Margaret Blume


Margaret "Peg" Blume, 85, of Harmar Township, formerly of Indianola, died Wednesday, May 30, 2007, at Harmar Village. She was born March 9
4 CONC , 1922, in Pittsburgh, daughter of the late James and Susan (Martin) Gaghan and resided in Indianola over 40 years before moving to Springdale. She was a self-employed hairdresser and member of St. Al
4 CONC phonsus Roman Catholic Church in Springdale. For years, Mrs. Blume was a Republican Committee Woman in Indiana Township. Survivors include her daughter, Dorothy (Donald) Shock, of Springdale Township;
4 CONC  sons, Gustave P. (Dorothy) Blume, of Springdale, James W. (Rose) Blume, of Denver, Colo., John M. Blume, of Monroeville, Joseph (Joyce) Blume, of Franklin, and Paul (Dawn) Blume, of State College; 18
4 CONC  grandchildren; eight great-grandchildren; and one sister, Shirley Kotchey, of Aspinwall. In addition to her parents, she was preceded in death by her husband, Gustave E. Blume, in 1980; two grandsons
4 CONC , Donald Shock Jr. and Paul Blume; also brothers and sisters. Friends will be received from 2 to 4 and 7 to 9 p.m. Friday at the CHARLES B. JARVIE FUNERAL HOME, Springdale. Christian Funeral Mass will
4 CONC  be celebrated at 10 a.m. Saturday in St. Alphonsus Church.

