1 TITL British Soldiers Died in the Great War, 1914 - 1919
1 PUBL MyHeritage
1 TEXT Each of the original volumes represented one or more regiments, corps or other units of the British Army. Most were subdivided into battalions or similar groupings. There were often thirty or more of 
2 CONC these per volume, each in alphabetical order. Information listed in these records may include: name, birth place, enlistment place, residence, number, decoration, rank, regiment, battalion, type of ca
2 CONC sualty, death date and death place.
