1 TITL New York State Deaths, 1957 - 1969
1 PUBL MyHeritage
1 TEXT Death certificates represent one of the key primary sources for family information, typically being issued within days of a death and having many details about a persons' life. Frequently, they contai
2 CONC n age, birthplace, parents' names and birthplaces and the cause of death. For deaths references in this index copies of original death certificates can be obtained from the <A href="http://www.health.
2 CONC ny.gov/vital_records/genealogy" target="_blank">New York State Department of Health</a> for a fee.
