1 TITL New Zealand, Death Index, 1840-2021
1 PUBL MyHeritage
1 TEXT Deaths have been officially recorded in New Zealand since 1848, and were originally under the jurisdiction of the Colonial Secretary. A law in 1913 required that Mäori deaths also be registered, and 
2 CONC these records were part of a separate registration system until 1961. The records in this collection are provided by the New Zealand <a id="" href="http://www.dia.govt.nz/" class="green" target="_blan
2 CONC k" rel="noopener">Department of Internal Affairs</a>.
1 _TYPE Collection
1 _MEDI 10972
0 @S500182@ SOUR
1 _UPD 4 OCT 2021 08:31:29 GMT -0500 
1 TITL New York City Marriage Index, 1866-1937
1 PUBL MyHeritage
1 TEXT This collection contains records for the following years per borough: 
2 CONC <ul><li>Bronx, 1898-1937</li><li>Brooklyn, 1866-1937</li><li>Manhattan, 1866-1937</li><li>Queens, 1905-1937 </li><li>Staten Island, 1898-1937</li></ul>
2 CONC Marriage records are an important genealogical record as they do not only record information about the bride, the groom, and their residence when the marriage occurred, but often contain additional in
2 CONC formation such as birth dates, birth places, occupations, and whether single, widowed, or divorced at the time of the marriage. Often a marriage license will also contain information about the parents
2 CONC  of the bride and groom including the parents’ names and birthplaces. Copies of the original marriage records in New York City are available for order for a fee from <a id="" href="http://www.nyc.go
2 CONC v/records" class="green">www.nyc.gov/records</a>. Marriages 50 or more years old are classified as public documents and are available to all researchers.
1 _TYPE Collection
1 _MEDI 10876
0 @S500183@ SOUR
1 _UPD 4 OCT 2021 08:31:57 GMT -0500 
