1 TITL Arlington National Cemetery
1 PUBL MyHeritage
1 TEXT Arlington National Cemetery was built during the American Civil War, established on May 13, 1864. The cemetery consists of 70 sections, including specific sections dedicated to those killed during the
2 CONC  War on Terror, military nurses, Confederate soldiers, former slaves, and other groups. Particularly from the 20th century to the present day, headstones often contain a religious symbol at the top, s
2 CONC uch as a Latin cross or a Star of David. The records in this collection are provided by <a id="" href="https://www.arlingtoncemetery.mil/#!/" class="green" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Arlington Nat
2 CONC ional Cemetery</a>.
